description:
Exploration question: Another agent will add an audit-log entry everywhere a user's role changes. Report what it has to touch, so it does not need to re-read these files.

Files read (every line is numbered as `line | code`; this is everything that has been read):

`src/admin/roles.ts`
```
1 | import { db } from "../db";
2 | 
3 | export async function setRole(userId: string, role: Role): Promise<void> {
4 |   await db.update("users", { role }, { id: userId });
5 | }
```

`src/invite/accept.ts`
```
1 | import { db } from "../db";
2 | 
3 | export async function acceptInvite(token: string, userId: string): Promise<void> {
4 |   const invite = await db.one("SELECT * FROM invites WHERE token = ?", [token]);
5 |   await db.update("users", { role: invite.role }, { id: userId });
6 |   await db.update("invites", { usedAt: new Date() }, { token });
7 | }
```

